# Cloudflare Pages _redirects: serve the single-file site for every real path.
# The client router reads location.pathname, so /books, /about, /blog and
# /blog/<slug> all load index.html and show the right page. /admin is the
# private login page (not linked anywhere public). Old #/ links are handled
# client-side by the router, which replaces them with the real path.
#
# WHY THIS FILE LISTS BOTH VARIANTS OF EVERY PATH
# Cloudflare Pages _redirects matching is exact per path: a rule for /books
# does NOT match /books/, and a rule for /books/ does NOT match /books.
# The previous version of this file listed only the no-slash form, so the
# trailing-slash form had no matching rule at all. Trailing-slash visits
# only worked by accident, through Pages' built-in SPA fallback (no top
# level 404.html, so Pages serves the root index.html for paths with no
# static asset), while no-slash visits were sent to the root / by Pages'
# clean-URL / route-matching handling before the router ever saw /books,
# so the router correctly showed Home for the / URL it was given. The
# client router itself was never the bug: routeFromPath strips trailing
# slashes and maps both /books and /books/ to the Books page.
# This file therefore lists both forms of every public path, plus a safe
# catch-all at the end, so neither form depends on the SPA fallback.
#
# DEPLOY NOTE: this file must sit at the REPO ROOT, next to index.html,
# sitemap.xml and functions/. It is NOT inside laketha-hicks-site.zip
# (the zip contains only index.html), so a zip-only deploy does NOT carry
# it. If it is missing from the deployed output, no-slash routes break
# again even though trailing-slash routes keep working via the SPA fallback.
#
# ORDER: first match wins, static rules before dynamic rules, and the
# catch-all /* must be LAST. Real static assets are listed first as
# self-rewrites so the catch-all can never swallow them. Requests handled
# by Pages Functions (/api/*) skip _redirects entirely, so the subscribe,
# login and posts endpoints are not affected by any rule here.
# Static assets: serve the file itself.
/assets/* /assets/:splat 200
/sitemap.xml /sitemap.xml 200
# Public pages: both the no-slash (canonical) form and the trailing-slash form.
/ /index.html 200
/books /index.html 200
/books/ /index.html 200
/about /index.html 200
/about/ /index.html 200
/speaking /index.html 200
/speaking/ /index.html 200
/faq /index.html 200
/faq/ /index.html 200
/blog /index.html 200
/blog/ /index.html 200
/blog/* /index.html 200
/contact /index.html 200
/contact/ /index.html 200
/admin /index.html 200
/admin/ /index.html 200
# Folded legacy pages (Portraits, Covers, Journey, Credentials now live
# inside About): both forms rewrite to index.html and the router shows About.
/portraits /index.html 200
/portraits/ /index.html 200
/covers /index.html 200
/covers/ /index.html 200
/journey /index.html 200
/journey/ /index.html 200
/credentials /index.html 200
/credentials/ /index.html 200
# Catch-all SPA fallback, LAST: any other path serves index.html with a
# 200 and the URL unchanged, so the client router can show the right page
# or fall back to Home. It cannot break /assets/*, /sitemap.xml or /api/*:
# /assets/* and /sitemap.xml matched their rules above, and /api/* is
# served by Pages Functions, which skip _redirects.
/* /index.html 200
